    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1517">

                <pb facs="1221" n="1105" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/515.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        Brown Brothers and Company and J. and W. Seligman and
                            Company to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegrams<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1517-f1"/> to us of Sept. 16th and Sept. 25th, and our telegrams to
                    you of Sept. 17th<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1517-f2"/> 25th<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1517-f3"/> and 26th, we beg to say that the negotiations with the
                    Government of Nicaragua therein referred to have resulted in an agreement
                    between the Republic and ourselves, dated November 4th, 1912, a copy<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1517-f4"/> of which we enclose herewith for your
                    information.</p>
                <p>In accordance with the provisions of this agreement, we have already released and
                    turned over to the Republic $100,000 of the customs moneys heretofore collected,
                    and out of the moneys received as the result of the Ethelburga Syndicate
                    settlement have set aside $400,000 which we now hold as a separate fund under
                    the agreement to be paid over to the Republic in installments at such times and
                    in such amounts as may be agreed upon between the President of the Republic and
                    us.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brown Brothers and Company</hi>. <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. and W. Seligman and Company.</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
